[quote="Foote"]

To be clear, the SotM card games has way more futures than Final Wasteland and Iron Legacy paths. First consider that, in an abstract sense, the multiverse contains infinity timelines where every possibility that can happen will happen, though I expect that this is not within the scope of what you would like to discuss. For more tangable &quot;dystopian&quot; futures, if we are casting a wide net on the term, consider the timeline Benchmark&#39;s Supply and Demand varient is from. A future where he is the only hero left alive would be on par with Wasteland or IL timelines in terms of &quot;oh crap-ness&quot;. And if we are counting Iron Legacy as a dystopian future, might we also consider the timeline that the alternate Luminary is from where Legacy is the bad guy and the female version of Baron is the hero? Something to consider.

[/quote]

I agree to everything you said, though i will edit my response about dystopian futures, that was more of a tongue in cheek fact. I&#39;m not expecting to get EVERY INFINITE timeline, but I should have specified, one&#39;s based on playable characters/villains/environments. This should include all variants (where applicable). Understanding the timelines in this is like explaining the X-Men timelines to someone wanting to get into it. I think simple is better then everything.&nbsp;

So, I&#39;ll update my original post to do the following:

1) Applicable to playable Environments/Heroes/Villains (variants included if applicable)

2) Non-dystopian futures as well

3) Must have enough background information to warrant attention. So, a timeline briefly mentioned in the flavour text may not count.

&nbsp;

Do you think this can be usefull, helpful, possible?&nbsp;

[quote="Foote"]

&nbsp;
<div class="bb-quote"><b>UXM266 wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">Can someone help me clarify Miss Information&#39;s timeline scenario?&nbsp;- Which universe did she die?- The version that &quot;replaced herself from a dimension which had overlapped &quot;our&quot; dimension due to ripples in the space/time continuum.&quot; is from which universe?- Does this mean there are three timelines with her? One where she&#39;s dead, one where she was replaced, and one where the replacement originally resided?&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
From all we can tell, the timeline where Miss Info dies is it&#39;s own seperate timeline and not attached to any other known/popular ones. I don&#39;t believe we have any evidence to suggest otherwise (at least not that I can recall).The timeline where she died overlapped with the &quot;main&quot; timeline that SotM focuses on. So in my estimation there are only two, not three, timelines in play here (the dieing and replacing happen together). She remembers dieing in our main timeline right? It&#39;s possible that she was never physically replaced but just caught glimpses and memories of herself from that other timeline. That much is unclear to me, but I still don&#39;t believe there are three versions in play either way.Aside from this, Miss Info shows a bunch of shenanigans in her Villains deck. It is not entirely clear if the visions she shows others are indeed of other timelines or just images conqured by her psychic powers. But there are multiple branches we can view if she is, in fact, showing other worlds. But that is a different topic I think.

[/quote]

Excellent! The timeline where she dies, and the one where she lives. the one where she lived through the sue of &quot;fancy space/time/magic/temporal stuff&quot; moved the the one where she died.&nbsp;

Thanks!
